      "reason": "Data revisions dismiss cached bar hover and reset/re-anchor time-series hover before position-only deduplication, preventing old values after polling. Touch end drops the saved finger position so refresh cannot resurrect a dismissed tooltip or crosshair. LTTB candidate buckets begin at the first interior observation and stop before the unique final endpoint, preserving early spikes. The host keeps tooltip-free plots pointer-inert for native vertical touch scrolling and uses full default timestamps for metric details."
    },
    {
      "files": ["charts/x-axis.tsx", "charts/bar-x-axis.tsx", "charts/y-axis.tsx"],
      "reason": "Native time/category axes limit tick density using actual inner width and align endpoint labels into the plot. Category labels reserve non-overlapping neighbour intervals, preserve both endpoints, and use bounded ellipsis with full title/tooltip/table text. Optional formatLabel abbreviates only the axis, not category identity. The adapter keeps UTC login buckets as canonical ISO keys, formats their axis/detail separately, and reserves space for byte-rate Y labels. Native numeric tick counts are bounded by actual scale range to avoid overlap in 120px metric cards. Compiled Chromium qualifies Korean/English/Japanese/Chinese clipping AND pairwise label collisions."
    },
    {
      "files": [
        "charts/host-config.tsx",
        "charts/time-series-chart-shell.tsx",
